From 86946ae0c2b5b43b752d58e060f36bdde085db7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 08:54:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Catchment preprocessing for REEF3D::HYDRO (W 10): hydrology
 cells from a DEM

catchment (catchment.h, catchment.cpp, catchment_flow.cpp, catchment_grid.cpp):
- catchment_dem.asc (ESRI ASCII grid), optional glacier, lake and zone rasters (W 30, 31, 32)
- priority flood (Barnes et al. 2014) with D8 flow directions: steepest lower neighbour, filled depressions
  and flats towards their spill point; the pop order is a topological order
- upstream area, catchment above the outlet (W 20), sub-catchments above the gauges (W 21), snapping (W 23)
- hydrology cells of W 11 m: area, equal-area elevation bands (W 12) with glacier fractions, outlet pixel,
  downstream cell along the fine flow path, channel length and slope (smallest W 24), zone, lake fraction
- output hydro_grid.dat (REEF3D R 100), DIVEMesh_Hydro/hydro_cells.vtk, hydro_network.vtk,
  catchment_fine.vtk (W 40 1)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
